{
  "schema_version": "1.0.0",
  "edition_id": "BSB",
  "book_code": "PSA",
  "chapter": 90,
  "verses": [
    {
      "id": "PSA.90.1",
      "edition_verse_id": "BSB:PSA.90.1",
      "verse": 1,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "A prayer of Moses the man of God. Lord, You have been our dwelling place through all generations.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": true
    },
    {
      "id": "PSA.90.2",
      "edition_verse_id": "BSB:PSA.90.2",
      "verse": 2,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Before the mountains were born or You brought forth the earth and the world, from everlasting to everlasting You are God.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "PSA.90.3",
      "edition_verse_id": "BSB:PSA.90.3",
      "verse": 3,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "You return man to dust, saying, “Return, O sons of mortals.”",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "PSA.90.4",
      "edition_verse_id": "BSB:PSA.90.4",
      "verse": 4,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "For in Your sight a thousand years are but a day that passes, or a watch of the night.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "PSA.90.5",
      "edition_verse_id": "BSB:PSA.90.5",
      "verse": 5,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "You sweep them away in their sleep; they are like the new grass of the morning—",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "PSA.90.6",
      "edition_verse_id": "BSB:PSA.90.6",
      "verse": 6,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "in the morning it springs up new, but by evening it fades and withers.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "PSA.90.7",
      "edition_verse_id": "BSB:PSA.90.7",
      "verse": 7,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "For we are consumed by Your anger and terrified by Your wrath.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "PSA.90.8",
      "edition_verse_id": "BSB:PSA.90.8",
      "verse": 8,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "You have set our iniquities before You, our secret sins in the light of Your presence.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "PSA.90.9",
      "edition_verse_id": "BSB:PSA.90.9",
      "verse": 9,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "For all our days decline in Your fury; we finish our years with a sigh.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "PSA.90.10",
      "edition_verse_id": "BSB:PSA.90.10",
      "verse": 10,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "The length of our days is seventy years — or eighty if we are strong — yet their pride is but labor and sorrow, for they quickly pass, and we fly away.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "PSA.90.11",
      "edition_verse_id": "BSB:PSA.90.11",
      "verse": 11,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Who knows the power of Your anger? Your wrath matches the fear You are due.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "PSA.90.12",
      "edition_verse_id": "BSB:PSA.90.12",
      "verse": 12,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "So teach us to number our days, that we may present a heart of wisdom.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "PSA.90.13",
      "edition_verse_id": "BSB:PSA.90.13",
      "verse": 13,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Return, O LORD! How long will it be? Have compassion on Your servants.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "PSA.90.14",
      "edition_verse_id": "BSB:PSA.90.14",
      "verse": 14,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Satisfy us in the morning with Your loving devotion, that we may sing for joy and be glad all our days.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "PSA.90.15",
      "edition_verse_id": "BSB:PSA.90.15",
      "verse": 15,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Make us glad for as many days as You have afflicted us, for as many years as we have seen evil.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "PSA.90.16",
      "edition_verse_id": "BSB:PSA.90.16",
      "verse": 16,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "May Your work be shown to Your servants, and Your splendor to their children.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "PSA.90.17",
      "edition_verse_id": "BSB:PSA.90.17",
      "verse": 17,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "May the favor of the Lord our God rest upon us; establish for us the work of our hands— yes, establish the work of our hands!",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    }
  ]
}
